<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    Kuna option itaniumeh (default on): a landing pad folded into the handler
    it jumps to still prints as a try region.

    The script loads the committed itaniumeh/eh4_x86_64.elf (g++ -O2, source
    eh4.cc beside it), the shape of patchelf's shrinkRPath:
    probe() makes a shared_ptr from readFile() inside a try that catches
    SysError. g++'s pads for operator new and for the Image constructor only
    load the exception registers and jump on into cleanup and catch code they
    share, so once the pad's own block is folded away, the arm the exceptional
    edge enters starts at that shared code, not at the pad's address.

    The printer took the pad from the arm's first instruction and printed
    both edges as `if (eh_unwinding()) { ... }` (#1). It now names the pad
    from the call-site record of the call the edge follows and finds the
    arm by the edge's own successor, so each prints as a try with a SysError
    catch (#2); the shared handler still rethrows unless errNo is ENOENT (#3).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/unlace-cli/tests/fixtures/itaniumeh/eh4_x86_64.elf</com>
  <com>option itaniumeh on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function probe</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="itaniumeh sharedpad #1: no exceptional edge to a folded pad prints as an if" min="0" max="0">if \(eh_unwinding\(\)\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="itaniumeh sharedpad #2: each pad of the try prints as a SysError catch" min="3" max="3">\} catch \(SysError\) \{</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="itaniumeh sharedpad #3: the shared handler rethrows unless errNo is ENOENT" min="1" max="1">__cxa_begin_catch\(v\d+\)\)\[2\] != 2\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
